{"name":"Boudin","hex":"#dab27d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boudin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of blood sausage in French, Belgian, Luxembourgish and related cuisines.","A sausage in southern Louisiana Creole and Cajun cuisine, made from rice, ground pork (occasionally crawfish), and spices in a sausage casing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boudin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boudin","blocks":[{"text":"Boudin is a category of sausage - typically blood sausage - found in several French-speaking cultures. The added ingredients vary in French, Luxembourgish, Belgian, Swiss, Québecois, Acadian, Aostan, Louisiana Creole, and Cajun cuisine. Some variations such as boudin blanc contain no blood but retain the name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Boudin3.jpg/330px-Boudin3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudin","wikidata":"Q13475519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/BoudinBallsElizabeths.jpg/500px-BoudinBallsElizabeths.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/BoudinBallsElizabeths.jpg/1280px-BoudinBallsElizabeths.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/BoudinBallsElizabeths.jpg/500px-BoudinBallsElizabeths.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"South Louisiana boudin balls","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoudinBallsElizabeths.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Boudin_Balls.jpg/250px-Boudin_Balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Boudin_Balls.jpg/500px-Boudin_B